<%# Layout for the square marketplace listing slides (hero, what's included,
    how it works, about).

    Separate from layouts/pdf_printable.html.erb on purpose. That layout is the
    printed product and is measured in inches and points; this one is a 1280px
    marketing canvas that is never printed. They shared a layout once — the
    gallery was the print sheet scaled to 0.73 on a square mat — and the result
    was honest but unsellable next to purpose-built competitor art.

    Ported from speakanyway-printables:
      src/templates/shared/branded-frame.css   -> the shared chrome below
      src/templates/previews/hero-board.css    -> .hero-*
      src/templates/previews/whats-included.css-> .included-*
      src/plugins/aac/templates/previews/about-saw.css -> .steps-strip, .founder-band

    Rails is authoritative for listings created from the Rails admin; that repo
    is authoritative for the ones its pipeline originates. They may differ —
    just not by accident. Same rule as Etsy::CopyRules.

    Three rails hold across every change here:

    1. Nothing is fetched over the network by the CHROME. Nunito is inlined by
       Boards::Printables::Fonts, and the logo, founder photo and room scenes by
       Boards::Printables::BrandAssets. The one documented exception is the
       board symbol art inside a page thumbnail, which loads from the CDN
       exactly as it does when the product PDF is printed.
    2. No emoji, and no decorative glyph outside Nunito's coverage. The render
       box's Chrome has no guaranteed colour-emoji font, so the pipeline's
       emoji step icons and its "*", "•" and arrow pseudo-element bullets would
       ship as tofu boxes to Etsy. Icons are inline SVG; bullets are CSS-drawn
       shapes. This repo already learned this once with U+2713 on the printed
       what's-included page.
    3. Every band is a fixed height and the copy that fills it is bounded
       (Printables::SlideCopy). Text that outgrows its band doesn't wrap here,
       it overlaps the next one. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Listing image</title>

    <style>
      <%= Boards::Printables::Fonts.face_css %>

      :root {
        --navy: #13496f;
        --blue-mid: #0163aa;
        --cyan: #4ECDE6;
        --magenta: #C857E8;
        --cream: #FBF7F1;
        --white: #FFFFFF;
        --ink: #1A1A1A;

        --brand-purple: #5b2a86;
        --brand-sky-deep: #79b8ec;
        --brand-green-soft: #c9f08a;

        --shadow-soft: 0 18px 40px rgba(19, 73, 111, 0.18);
        --shadow-card: 0 24px 56px rgba(19, 73, 111, 0.28);
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      html, body {
        -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
        print-color-adjust: exact;
      }

      body {
        font-family: Nunito, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: var(--cream);
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      p, li { text-wrap: pretty; hyphens: none; }

      /* ── The canvas ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      /* Etsy shows listing photos in a square frame and letterboxes anything
         else, so the slide IS square rather than being cropped to one. */
      .slide {
        position: relative;
        width: 1280px;
        height: 1280px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: var(--cream);
      }

      /* Background photo as an <img>, not a CSS url() — the src is a data URI
         and this keeps the encoding in one place (BrandAssets). */
      .slide .bg-image {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        z-index: 0;
      }

      /* The room photos are bright and busy; without this the navy title and
         the white paper cards both lose contrast against a sunlit window. */
      .slide .bg-scrim {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        z-index: 1;
        background: linear-gradient(
          180deg,
          rgba(251, 247, 241, 0.88) 0%,
          rgba(251, 247, 241, 0.42) 34%,
          rgba(251, 247, 241, 0.62) 72%,
          rgba(251, 247, 241, 0.90) 100%
        );
      }

      .slide.bg-sky {
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at 20% 18%, rgba(255,255,255,0.9) 0 110px, transparent 140px),
          radial-gradient(circle at 78% 22%, rgba(255,255,255,0.75) 0 70px, transparent 110px),
          linear-gradient(180deg, #b9e2ff 0%, #dff0ff 60%, #f7fbff 100%);
      }

      /* ── Slide stack ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      /* Everything except the hero lays out as a flex column rather than a set
         of absolutely-positioned bands at hand-tuned offsets. The bands drift:
         a board with a long name grows its card, an overflow caption appears
         only for a set, and the fixed offsets that looked right for one
         printable had the caption colliding with a tile label on the next.
         A column can't collide with itself. */
      .slide-stack {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        z-index: 4;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
        gap: 20px;
        padding: 52px 56px 56px;
      }

      /* The footer strip is anchored to the bottom edge, so the column has to
         stop above it. */
      .slide-stack.has-footer { padding-bottom: 214px; }

      .slide-stack > * { flex: 0 0 auto; max-width: 100%; }

      /* The one element that absorbs the leftover height, so a short board and
         a tall one both produce a balanced slide. */
      .slide-stack > .stretch {
        flex: 1 1 auto;
        min-height: 0;
        width: 100%;
      }

      /* ── Shared chrome ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .logo-corner {
        position: absolute;
        z-index: 5;
        top: 34px;
        right: 34px;
        width: 108px;
        height: 108px;
      }

      .title-banner {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 4;
        display: inline-block;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 20px 36px;
        background: var(--navy);
        color: var(--white);
        border-radius: 18px;
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 52px;
        line-height: 1.05;
        max-width: 880px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
      }

      .title-banner.small { font-size: 44px; }

      .headline-callout {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 4;
        display: inline-block;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 16px 30px;
        background: var(--white);
        color: var(--ink);
        border-radius: 14px;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 32px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
      }

      /* The one claim that answers "do I have to wait for this in the post?" */
      .instant-ribbon {
        position: absolute;
        z-index: 6;
        top: 0;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        padding: 16px 56px;
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--white);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 25px;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .slide.has-ribbon .title-banner { margin-top: 96px; }

      .accent-panel {
        position: absolute;
        z-index: 4;
        border-radius: 18px;
        padding: 26px 30px;
        color: var(--white);
        background: var(--brand-purple);
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 27px;
        line-height: 1.25;
      }

      .accent-panel .accent-eyebrow {
        display: block;
        font-size: 17px;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        opacity: 0.85;
        margin-bottom: 6px;
      }

      .accent-panel .accent-sub {
        display: block;
        margin-top: 10px;
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 21px;
        opacity: 0.95;
      }

      /* ── CSS-drawn bullets (never a glyph) ────────────────────────────── */
      .bullets { list-style: none; }

      .bullets li {
        position: relative;
        padding-left: 30px;
      }

      .bullets li::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 0.55em;
        width: 14px;
        height: 14px;
        border-radius: 4px;
        transform: rotate(45deg);
        background: var(--brand-purple);
      }

      .bullets.on-dark li::before { background: var(--brand-green-soft); }

      /* ── Footer strip ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .footer-strip {
        position: absolute;
        z-index: 4;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        min-height: 190px;
        padding: 26px 56px;
        background: var(--brand-green-soft);
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 34px;
      }

      .footer-strip .footer-bullets { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }

      .footer-strip .footer-title {
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 25px;
        letter-spacing: 0.03em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      .footer-strip ul { font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.5; }

      .footer-strip .footer-qr {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8px;
      }

      .footer-strip .footer-qr img {
        width: 132px;
        height: 132px;
        padding: 7px;
        background: var(--white);
        border-radius: 12px;
      }

      .footer-strip .footer-qr .qr-caption {
        font-size: 17px;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      /* ── Paper card: how a board page is presented on every slide ─────── */
      /* The thumbnail arrives already trimmed to its content
         (RenderPageThumbnails), so the card hugs the page rather than forcing
         it to a fixed box — height is driven by the image's own aspect and
         capped by the slot. A white sheet with a shadow is what makes it read
         as a printed page. */
      .paper {
        background: var(--white);
        border-radius: 10px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
        overflow: hidden;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-self: center;
      }

      .paper img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        max-height: 100%;
        object-fit: contain;
        background: var(--white);
      }

      .paper .paper-label {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        padding: 8px 10px;
        background: var(--navy);
        color: var(--white);
        font-size: 20px;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-align: center;
        white-space: nowrap;
        overflow: hidden;
        text-overflow: ellipsis;
      }

      /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      /* The ribbon overlays the top edge, so the hero's column starts below it. */
      .slide-stack.has-ribbon { padding-top: 108px; }

      .hero-stage {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 22px;
      }

      .hero-stage .paper { flex: 1 1 0; max-height: 100%; }

      /* A single page gets the whole stage. */
      .hero-stage.single .paper { max-width: 1000px; }

      /* A set fans into an overlapping pile rather than a tidy row. Three
         side-by-side cards on a 1168px stage are ~370px wide, and a board page
         at that size is a coloured smudge — the buyer can count the pages but
         can't see a single word. Overlapping buys each card ~50% more width
         and reads as "more than one board" just as fast. */
      /* The widths have to close: three cards at W overlapping by V occupy
         3W - 2V, and anything over 100% runs the outer pages off the slide
         edge. 40% and 11% land at 98% and leave room for the rotation to
         bleed without clipping. */
      .hero-stage.fan { gap: 0; }
      .hero-stage.fan .paper { flex: 0 0 40%; }

      .hero-stage.fan .paper:nth-child(1) {
        transform: rotate(-3deg);
        margin-right: -11%;
        z-index: 1;
      }

      .hero-stage.fan .paper:nth-child(2) { z-index: 3; }

      .hero-stage.fan .paper:nth-child(3) {
        transform: rotate(3deg);
        margin-left: -11%;
        z-index: 2;
      }

      .hero-empty {
        font-size: 30px;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
        background: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);
        border-radius: 18px;
        padding: 40px 48px;
        text-align: center;
      }

      /* ── What's included ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .tile-grid {
        display: grid;
        gap: 18px;
        align-content: center;
        justify-items: center;
      }

      .tile-grid .paper { min-height: 0; max-height: 100%; }

      .overflow-note {
        width: 100%;
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 25px;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      .included-panel {
        width: 100%;
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--white);
        border-radius: 18px;
        padding: 24px 30px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
      }

      .included-panel .included-title {
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 27px;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
      }

      .included-panel ul { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.5; }

      /* ── How it works ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      /* Sized by its copy, not by the slide. Stretching the strip makes four
         600px-tall white cards with two lines of text at the top of each. */
      .steps-strip {
        width: 100%;
        display: flex;
        align-items: stretch;
        gap: 20px;
        margin-top: 26px;
      }

      .step-card {
        position: relative;
        flex: 1;
        background: var(--white);
        border-radius: 22px;
        padding: 46px 22px 26px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
        text-align: center;
      }

      .step-card .step-num {
        position: absolute;
        top: -24px;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translateX(-50%);
        width: 54px;
        height: 54px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--brand-purple);
        color: var(--white);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 27px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
      }

      /* Inline SVG, never an emoji — see rail 2 at the top of this file. */
      .step-card .step-icon {
        width: 62px;
        height: 62px;
        margin: 0 auto 12px;
        display: block;
        fill: none;
        stroke: var(--blue-mid);
        stroke-width: 5;
        stroke-linecap: round;
        stroke-linejoin: round;
      }

      .step-card .step-title {
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 27px;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      .step-card .step-body {
        font-size: 19px;
        line-height: 1.4;
        color: #333;
      }

      /* Groups the elements that should stay together and centres them in the
         leftover height as one block, instead of each one finding its own
         corner and leaving a hole in the middle of the slide. */
      .band-group {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 44px;
      }

      .qr-block {
        width: 100%;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 24px;
      }

      .qr-block .qr-prompt {
        background: var(--navy);
        color: var(--white);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 27px;
        padding: 14px 22px;
        border-radius: 14px;
      }

      .qr-block img {
        width: 168px;
        height: 168px;
        padding: 9px;
        background: var(--white);
        border-radius: 14px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
      }

      /* ── About ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      /* Hugs its copy and floats in the middle of what's left, rather than
         stretching: a stretched band is a 700px-tall white card with three
         lines of text marooned in the centre of it. */
      .founder-band {
        width: 100%;
        margin: auto 0;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 40px;
        padding: 44px 40px;
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
        border-radius: 24px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
      }

      /* Fixed square so the row can't reflow if the photo is swapped for one
         with a different aspect; object-position sits above centre because the
         source is a head-and-shoulders crop and dead centre cuts the forehead. */
      .founder-photo {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        width: 230px;
        height: 230px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        object-fit: cover;
        object-position: 50% 38%;
        border: 5px solid var(--white);
        box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(19, 73, 111, 0.22);
      }

      .founder-copy { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }

      .founder-hi {
        font-size: 36px;
        font-weight: 800;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        color: var(--brand-purple);
      }

      .founder-copy p {
        font-size: 23px;
        line-height: 1.45;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
      }

      .founder-copy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; font-weight: 700; }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
